{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (62.71%) to LL-37 A hybrid peptide consisting of full length LL-37 and ranalexin are connected via a GS linker. Activity: active against S. aureus MRSA (MIC 17.5-20.1 uM), E. coli (MIC 19.7-21.4 uM), and K. pneumoniae (MIC 27.8 uM) bacteria clinical isolates. Recombinant production:bacteria:Escherichia coli: expressed as a fusion with small metal-binding proteins SmbP or CusF3H+. cleaved with enzyme enterokinase, Purified via immobilized metal affinity chromatography, peptide yield: 0.7-2.1 mg/L after affinity column.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38229302", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Appl Microbiol Biotechnol. 2024 Dec;108(1):126. doi: 10.1007/s00253-023-12887-5. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04037", "source_id": "AP04037", "source_numeric_id": "04037", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04037", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "LL-37_Renalexin hybrid peptide exhibits antimicrobial activity at lower MICs than its counterpart single peptides.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
